      "content": "The US got involved in Vietnam to contain the spread of communism, a policy that many historians now argue was a catastrophic failure of the Cold War mindset. While the initial goal was to prevent a domino effect across Southeast Asia, the war ultimately resulted in massive American casualties and a humiliating defeat that exposed the limits of military force against a determined insurgency. Modern historical consensus largely views the conflict as a tragic mistake where the US overestimated its ability to impose its will on a sovereign nation, leading to deep domestic division and a lasting legacy of distrust in government.",
